[size=4][b]Overview[/b][/size]
Magic Menu Rewrite is an SKSE plugin that reworks the SkyUI magic menu.
It keeps the SkyUI spell list as is, and rebuilds the space next to it using blocks.
Works on Skyrim SE and AE. VR is not supported.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]3D Preview: Shows the 3D model of the selected spell in a box next to the list.
[*]Spell Card: Shows the school, skill level, magicka cost, cast type, duration, and description.
[*]Block Layout: Each panel is a block, set in two columns. Each column scrolls on its own. Press K to turn on edit mode and drag blocks to where you want them. Press Backspace in edit mode to return to the default layout. The layout is saved across all characters.
[*]Hotkey Prompts: Menu hotkeys are shown on the SkyUI bottom bar.
[*]Add-on Blocks: Other SKSE plugins can add their own blocks to the menu (Block API).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Heart of Magic Block (Optional, in Heart of Magic Librarian)[/b][/size]
This block is for Heart of Magic Librarian users. Starting in 1.2.0, it comes with Heart of Magic Librarian 1.9.0 and you can select it on the "Magic Menu Rewrite" page of its installer.
Update both on the same day: with Magic Menu Rewrite 1.2.0 and Heart of Magic Librarian older than 1.9.0, the block is gone from the menu unless the 1.1.0 copy is still installed. A saved layout keeps the block's place while it is away, and `MagicMenuRewrite.ini` keeps the block's keys.
[list]
[*]Spell Tree Panel: Shows where the selected spell is on the tree and what spells are around it. Hover to see the description, and click a spell to show it in the card and 3D box. You can also view spells you have not learned yet.
[*]Learning Progress Card: Shows your learning target and progress for each school, along with spells you can learn right now. With no learning target, it lists the spells you can learn next (those after the spell you just mastered first); click one to make it your learning target.
[*]Node Card: Shows the status and prerequisites of the selected spell, and has a button to set it as your learning target.
[*]Hotkeys: U jumps to the next spell you can learn, and G sets that spell as your learning target.
[/list]
(You can choose which blocks are shown in the SKSE Menu Framework settings menu.)

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]SKSE64
[*]Address Library for SKSE Plugins
[*]SkyUI
[/list]

[size=4][b]Optional Mods[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Heart of Magic Librarian: 1.9.0 or later installs the Heart of Magic block (select the "Magic Menu Rewrite" option in its installer).
[*]SKSE Menu Framework: Needed to use the in-game settings menu. (Note for Korean players: set EnableKorean = true in SKSEMenuFramework.ini to show Korean in the settings menu.)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Installing with a mod manager opens the FOMOD installer.
Core files (always installed). The installer's "Add-on blocks" page is gone; blocks for other mods now ship with their own mods.

[size=4][b]Settings and Language[/b][/size]
Supports English and Korean. The language is selected automatically to match your game language.
It also shows Korean if you use a Korean patch on an English copy of the game.
If you have SKSE Menu Framework, you can choose the language and which blocks to show in the in-game settings menu.
Without it, you can change the same settings in MagicMenuRewrite.ini.
Settings chosen in the menu are saved separately, so they stay when you update the mod.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Inventory Reforged: Includes a config file that turns off Inventory Reforged's magic menu panel so both mods do not edit the magic menu at the same time. If you changed this setting yourself in Inventory Reforged, your choice is kept. Uninstalling this mod brings back the Inventory Reforged panel.
[*]Confirmed working with the Untarnished UI bottom bar and STB Hotkey System hotkey prompts.
[*]Other screen shapes and UI skins: if SkyUI's list reaches into the blocks' area, the area moves right when the menu opens (and gets narrower if the screen has little room).
[/list]
The Spell Research block will come with Spell Research - Prisma UI 2 (not released yet; its page will come later).

[size=4][b]For Modders[/b][/size]
Other SKSE plugins can add their own block to the menu through the Block API. The optional file "Magic Menu Rewrite - Modder Resources" has the guide (BLOCK_API_GUIDE.md), the header (BlockApi.h) and an example plugin you can build.

